Let $\begin{aligned}$I &amp; =$\int \frac{d x}{(x+100) \sqrt{x+99}}$\\
&amp; =$\int \frac{d x}{\left.(\sqrt{x+99})^2+1\right) \sqrt{x+99}}
\end{aligned}$Put $\sqrt{x+99}=t \Rightarrow \frac{1}{\sqrt{x+99}} d x=2 d t\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad$I &amp; =$\int \frac{2 d t}{t^2+1}=$2 \tan ^{-1} t+c \\
&amp; =2 \tan ^{-1} $\sqrt{x+99}+$c
\end{aligned} From Eqs. (i) $\begin{gathered}$2 \tan ^{-1} $\sqrt{x+99}+$c=f(x)+c \\
f(x)=2 \tan ^{-1} $\sqrt{x+99}
\end{gathered}$
